<title>NORWAY: BNbank shares jump on merger proposal.</title>
<headline>BNbank shares jump on merger proposal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The share price of Norway's Bolig og Naeringsbanken (BNbank) jumped on Tuesday following a merger proposal from Norway's fourth largest bank, Fokus Bank ASA.</p>
<p>BNbank, a niche institution specialising in mortgage loans, was up 25 crowns at 192 crowns at 1015 GMT on the Oslo Bourse in healthy turnover of more than 61 million crowns.</p>
<p>Fokus was up 1.50 crowns at 60 crowns in turnover worth 31 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
